5 was also recorded in parts of Aichi, Shizuoka, Gifu and Nagano prefectures. The earthquake shattered storefront windows, knocked merchandise from shelves and disrupted regional train services, including Shinkansen bullet trains, which were delayed or operated at reduced speeds for safety checks. No tsunami warning was issued, and no abnormalities were detected at the Hamaoka nuclear power plant in Shizuoka, according to its operator, Chubu Electric Power Co. Following the earthquake, JMA official Ayataka Ebita warned residents to remain alert for further strong tremors over the coming week, particularly during the next two to three days. He also cautioned that rainfall could increase the risk of landslides and falling rocks in areas affected by strong shaking. Regarding the Nankai Trough, where a major earthquake is considered possible, the agency said no apparent changes hadbeen detected following Sunday's tremor. Meanwhile, a separate 4.3-magnitude earthquake struck Kumamoto Prefecture in southwestern Japan later Sunday morning, with no immediate reports of serious damage or injuries. Japan lies along the Pacific Ring of Fire, one of the world's most seismically active regions.ns, making it particularly vulnerable to earthquake", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["world"], "creator": ["agencies"], "language": "english", "country": ["saudi arabia"], "category": ["world"], "datatype": "news", "pubDate": "2026-11-08 12:44:30", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-11-08 13:15:41", "image_url": "https://saudigazette.com.sa/saudigazette/uploads/images/2026/11/08/2791495.webp", "video_url": null, "source_id": "saudigazette", "source_name": "Saudi Gazette", "source_priority": 356263, "source_url": "https://saudigazette.com.sa", "source_icon": "https://i.newsdata.io/saudigazette.png", "sentiment": "negative", "sentiment_stats": {"negative": 95.55, "neutral": 3.76, "positive": 0.69}, "ai_tag": ["natural disasters", "accidents"], "ai_region": "ONLY